  id: W3_01
  era: Completed 1010 CE
  title: Brihadisvara Temple, Thanjavur
  text: 'Brihadisvara Temple, Thanjavur. Raja Raja I, the great Chola emperor, built this temple to Shiva at his capital Thanjavur. Its tower rises about 66 metres and is crowned by a huge granite capstone. Inscriptions on its walls list the gifts, dancers, musicians and staff that served the temple. The Cholas were also a sea power: Raja Raja''s son Rajendra sent a naval expedition to South-East Asia, and Chola merchants traded as far as China.'
